— the direct hardcoded-version request, and the platform's endorsed constraint reached transitively through the relocation — and Gradle can't reconcile them. This reproduces deterministically for anyone declaring a hardcoded version on the legacy coordinate; it isn't flaky or environment-specific.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1 transitively pulls in org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-platform (endorseStrictVersions=true), whose Gradle module metadata constrains the same legacy org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial coordinate the scaffold hardcodes a version for, so Gradle reports conflicting version constraints and fails before compilation/native-image ever run.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Do not leave the generated dependency as a bare hardcoded-version `testImplementation \\\"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\\\"` for 8.0.0.Beta1 — it will hit Gradle's 'Component is the target of multiple version constraints with conflicting requirements' error because hibernate-spatial transitively depends on org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-platform, which itself constrains the same legacy org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial GA back to the same version. Work around it in build.gradle, e.g.: `testImplementation(\\\"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\\\") { exclude group: 'org.hibernate.orm', module: 'hibernate-platform' }`, or declare the dependency directly under the new coordinate `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion` instead of the legacy relocated one. Confirm the chosen fix still resolves cleanly and doesn't hide a real version conflict among other hibernate-orm submodules pulled in transitively (hibernate-core, etc.).\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"This is hibernate-orm's first 8.x Beta; the self-referencing platform constraint may be a publishing artifact of the new modularized build that changes or disappears in later Beta/RC/Final releases — re-verify the exact conflict shape rather than assuming this workaround still applies to a newer version.\",\n    \"Excluding hibernate-platform from the dependency could suppress intended version alignment across other transitive hibernate-orm modules; check for new conflicts after applying the exclusion.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":14273,"type":"result","duration_ms":208903,"uuid":"c2964333-05c6-4083-9a38-456c0de1e535","ttft_stream_ms":1067,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":1067,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

